// parents. One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner takes part in the mediated agreement meeting at
// Vahtra 5 (community mediator Helve Sild) and writes an apology and agreement letter (049 Kasuta).
// Grammar (B2, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5): the clitic -ki / -gi and indefinite pronouns — keegi, miski / midagi,
// kunagi, kuskil, mitte keegi / mitte kunagi, ka tema → temagi, isegi, „after all” (ta tuligi, ma ei vastanudki) —
// taught in 047 (notice, rule table, meanings sorted; gaps, transformation, cloze; used in the Kasuta call and mail),
// back in 049 (negotiation phrases, word order, the final letter); 048 trains reported speech and the quotative (-vat).
// Harno B2 formats and the final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1 row 10, 2026-10-29): 046 LUGE R→W (corner
// R1 = the reader survey „Mida me naabrilt ootame?”, ≈ 560 words, predict and check; main = W14 recommendation to Gert:
// both candidates' strengths and weaknesses with examples and a reasoned conclusion, ≈ 180 words), 047 RÄÄK R→S (corner
// W1 = Gert's angry mail rewritten as a semi-formal note to Liis, 80–100 words; main = S16 talk at Hendrik's meeting,
// recorded at home), 048 KIRJ L→W (corner R2b = the class teacher's letter, eight answers of 1–3 words; main = W13
// semi-formal letter to the class teacher), 049 PROJ L→S (corner S2 = the quiet-hours debate with argument cards A / B;
// main = the mediated agreement meeting at Vahtra 5, S03). Every teaching lesson: review naming the previous lesson and
// a module 6–8 lesson, a pair task in the lesson, a home recording in Kasuta, two fluency tasks; S16 in 046 and 047, S17
// in 046 and 049. Module 9's words return: toitumine, menüü, suhkur, allergia, harjumus, muutuma, tervislik, uni,
